    "note": "The framing group does not reach 1.000 and cannot. Seven of the eight accepted corruptions turned a valid MTI into another valid MTI, which a parser must accept. The eighth flipped one bitmap bit and swapped DE 14 for DE 16 - both n4, so the layout is byte-identical and the message re-parses as a different, entirely well-formed message. An ISO 8583 bitmap carries no redundancy, so no parser can catch that. It is the reason the invariant layer exists rather than stopping at the codec."
